Slow-mopolis thing, yeah.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.500
I'm always fascinated by how

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.880
when you film something in slow motion,

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.670
it kind of adds scale to it.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.720
It makes everything seem a bit weightier.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.940
Is that what they do on
Thunderbirds and stuff like that?

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.260
Yeah and like Independence Day,

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.310
it had a lot of model shots.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.143
That's cool.

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:18.976
So, what are we doing with this

00:00:18.976 --> 00:00:19.809
lovely little town we've built?

00:00:19.809 --> 00:00:22.130
We've got a town, it
took us ages to build.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:22.963
It was about a three hour build.

00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:24.320
You wouldn't think it, but it did.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.330
Got a plane.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.230
Gonna crash it through
the back of Slow-mopolis

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.280
and hopefully, get some cool shots.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.280
There's a plane right now.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.470
Yeah.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.620
See you later, go on.

00:00:34.572 --> 00:00:35.770
Hopefully, we get some quite cool shots

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.700
of bits exploding everywhere,
people going flying,

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.180
buildings collapsing that sort will do.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.030
Yeah, the pilot is unaware

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:44.160
he's about to have an
engine failure at six feet.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.190
Six feet?
Six feet.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.600
That's deadly that.
Deadly, lethal.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.410
This guy's got no idea either,
he's just having a brew.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.840
Yeah.
Just chillin'.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.490
All right, let's see how we get on.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:52.323
Cool.

00:00:52.323 --> 00:00:53.660
Wanna explain what happened
last time we did this?

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.533
Well basically the plane,

00:00:56.461 --> 00:00:58.640
there's no where good to
hold it under the wings

